ai_context: >-
  Benchmark evidence database for the omni-benchmark LiveSQLBench evaluation.
  Grain: one attempt per row in neondb_telemetry__attempt, keyed by attempt_id
  and generation_record_sha256. Use arm (C1, C2, C3, C4, C5, E02, R2-C5B,
  R2-M1) as the analysis unit; condition is the preregistered condition and
  stores C5 and E02 as C4. Correctness exists only for partition dev-a, in
  neondb_telemetry__score, with two frozen scorers that are always reported
  together: official_soft_ex (benchmark-comparable) and sensitivity. Accuracy
  is correct divided by status = scored rows of that scorer. Sealed test
  attempts (partition test) carry telemetry only; their published rates live
  in neondb_telemetry__sealed_aggregate. Prefer the modeled measures over
  reconstructing them. Cross-arm accuracy comparisons across C1 through C5 must
  be filtered to neondb_telemetry__dev_a_frame.in_official_frame (122
  questions) or in_sensitivity_frame (121 questions); unfiltered per-arm
  denominators are not comparable because the arms did not all run the same
  questions. R2-C5B and R2-M1 are a separate paired study over 136 dev-A
  questions, a superset of both frames, so a frame filter changes their counts
  away from the frozen R2 rollup; say which set a number is over. Cost comes in
  three kinds and they must never be blurred. Measured: account-wide Omni AI
  spend per billing period in neondb_telemetry__credit_period, where one credit
  is one dollar. Estimated: the per-arm allocation of that spend in
  neondb_telemetry__arm_cost, basis proportional_estimate. Its lower rate divides
  account spend across all AI conversations and assumes one conversation per
  attempt; its upper rate allocates all account spend across recorded attempts.
  Both recorded rates are rounded and assume attempts cost the same.
  Unmeasured: per-attempt cost_usd on neondb_telemetry__attempt, which is NULL
  for every governed arm because the credit-bracketing path was not armed for
  those runs; cost_unavailable_reason says so per attempt. Never estimate cost
  from token counts, and never present an arm_cost figure as a measurement.
